      "math_academy_id": "q-22354",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "A solution to the linear equation $y=3x-2$ is the ordered pair $(4,t).$ What is the value of $t?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $(4,t)$ is a solution to the linear equation $y=3x-2,$ the equation must turn into a true statement if we substitute $4$ and $t$ for $x$ and $y.$ So, we replace $x$ with $4$ and $y$ with $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x-2 \\\\ (t) & =3(4)-2 \\\\ t & =12-2 \\\\ t & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$",
